## The answer to the open question

The first attempt blocked on C6 of the Red test, and on the vertical centring of the titles. The
orchestrator answered on 2026-11-11: do not use 2 fixed em shifts. Center the ink box of each title
exactly, from a letter extent table. It is the same method as the advance width table of r2b.

## The letter extent table

The script `measure/runs/storytime_cover_options_20261106/league-spartan-extents-r2c.mjs` is a copy
of `league-spartan-widths-r2b.mjs` with the measure part and the output changed. It records, for the
95 ASCII characters 32 to 126 at 1000 px, `actualBoundingBoxAscent / 1000` and
`actualBoundingBoxDescent / 1000`. It records also `measureText('H').actualBoundingBoxAscent`
(0.6719), `fontBoundingBoxAscent` (0.70), and `fontBoundingBoxDescent` (0.22). The launch timeout
stays 30 s, and `browser.close()` stands in a `finally` block.

One heavy-run with `HEAVY_RUN_TIMEOUT_S=300` exits 0 and prints 95 ascents, 95 descents, the cap, and
the 2 font values. The capture is `league-spartan-extents-r2c.txt`.

Deviation D-1: one committed generator script ran Chrome once in heavy-run with a 300 s limit to
make the letter extent table (orchestrator decision 2026-11-11).

## The code

`dashboard/lib/storytime/print/cover-quest.ts`:

- E1 to E11 of the readers r2c Red, from the patch `green-readers-r2c-blocked-impl.patch`: the A3
  week pill and role bar letters at 80 % of the inner height, the pill hugging its text with even
  padding and 340 mm centring, the leaf plaque in the K palette from the r2 book plaque drawing, the
  leaf footer, and the band check export of the build script.
- The measured extent tables `LEAGUE_SPARTAN_700_ASCENT` and `LEAGUE_SPARTAN_700_DESCENT` (95
  values each), `LEAGUE_SPARTAN_700_CAP` (0.6719), `LEAGUE_SPARTAN_700_FONT_ASCENT` (0.70), and
  `LEAGUE_SPARTAN_700_FONT_DESCENT` (0.22). `LEAGUE_SPARTAN_CAP_EM` takes the measured cap. Every
  one has JSDoc, and the JSDoc names the script.
- `titleInkEm(text)` gives the ink top (the larger of the cap and the largest table ascent of the
  characters) and the ink bottom (the largest table descent). A character outside the table counts
  as the cap ascent and 0 descent.
- `titleCapFontMm(bandMm)` gives the font whose cap height is 80 % of the band. The A3 title takes
  40.96 mm, the leaf title 17.15 mm, and the front row 10.00 mm.
- `titleLineTopMm(text, fontMm, bandTopMm, bandMm, lines)` places the baseline by the line box: the
  baseline lies `(1 - A - D) / 2 + A` em below the top of the 1 em line box, that is 0.74 em. The
  top is set so that the ink centre stands at the band centre. The A3 title, the leaf title, and the
  front row use it, and the 2-line case of B5 uses it with the grown band. `TITLE_SHIFT_EM`,
  `TITLE_DESCENDER_SHIFT_EM`, `hasDescenderLetter`, and `titleShiftMm` are gone.
- The leaf plaque width is the title width plus 2 x 21 mm, at least 110 mm and at most 182 mm,
  centered on the 198 mm page. The top 113 mm and the height 20 mm stay.
- The front plaque width with hlogo is the row width plus 2 x 16 mm, at least 158 mm, centered on
  the 210 mm page. The top 278 mm and the height 14 mm stay. The box table does not change.
- With hlogo, the teacher front renders no `band-pill` part. The box `teacher-front:band-pill` and
  the default render of the pill stay.
- With hlogo, the student back panel takes `text-align:center` on its headings and its values. Its
  box, its padding, and its font sizes stay.
- The JSDoc of every changed function names the round of 2026-11-11.

`dashboard/scripts/storytime/make-storytime-quest-covers.ts`: the `bandCheck` reader leaf branch
passes a leaf with the logo tile that holds no band word part and no band word, and the script
exports `questBandCheck`. The JSDoc is updated.

